<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>On a map of scale <m>1 : {1000}</m>, the outline of the compound of a school in Machakos is drawn on a grid of <m>1\,\text{cm}</m> squares. Kiprono counts <m>{32}</m> full squares and <m>{18}</m> part squares.</p><p>(a) Estimate the area of the outline in squares.</p><div><fillin characters="8" name="ans1"/> squares  </div><p>(b) What real length, in metres, does the side of one square stand for?</p><div><fillin characters="8" name="ans2"/> <m>\text{m}</m>  </div><p>(c) What real area does one square stand for?</p><div><fillin characters="10" name="ans3"/> <m>\text{m}^2</m>  </div><p>(d) Estimate the area of the compound of a school in Machakos in hectares (<m>1</m> hectare <m>= 10\,000\,\text{m}^2</m>), correct to 2 decimal places.</p><div><fillin characters="8" name="ans4"/> ha  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) Each part square counts as half a square: <m>{32} + \tfrac{1}{2} \times {18} = {41}</m> squares.</p><p>(b) <m>1\,\text{cm}</m> on the map stands for <m>{1000}\,\text{cm}</m> on the ground, which is <m>{1000} \div 100 = {10}\,\text{m}</m>.</p><p>(c) A square on the map stands for a square on the ground, so square the real length of its side: <m>{10} \times {10} = {100}\,\text{m}^2</m>.</p><p>(d) Area <m>\approx {41} \times {100} = {4100}\,\text{m}^2</m>. Divide by <m>10\,000</m> to change to hectares: about <m>{0.41}</m> ha, correct to 2 decimal places.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>41</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>10</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>100</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{41}{100}</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>